# Recyclarr Configuration
#
# DON'T edit this file directly. Instead, generate configs from templates:
#
#   docker exec recyclarr recyclarr config create -t web-1080p -t hd-bluray-web
#
# This creates files under /srv/recyclarr/config/configs/ with proper TRaSH profiles.
# Edit each generated file to set base_url and api_key, then sync:
#
#   docker exec recyclarr recyclarr sync
#
# List all available templates:
#   docker exec recyclarr recyclarr config list templates
#
# Sonarr templates: web-1080p, web-2160p, web-1080p-alternative, ...
# Radarr templates: hd-bluray-web, remux-web-1080p, uhd-bluray-web, ...
#
# Sonarr API key: Settings -> General -> API Key (http://SERVER_IP:8989)
# Radarr API key: Settings -> General -> API Key (http://SERVER_IP:7878)
